        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; event-level conclusion remains unverified\n\nThe relevant order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Required detail | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Unavailable |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event record and event type |\n\nThe available task records contain **no `work_order_cost_events` rows**. The supporting-record service returned **“404 — supporting records not staged”**, and its access metadata limits reads to a records custodian. No authorized release became available. This missing evidence **does not establish that no late event occurred**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” printed page 225 (PDF page 233)**, states that new transactions created after Pending Close, relating to the current or a prior period, are not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue processing.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary new manufacturing transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held from processing while September remains Pending Close. I cannot compare that rule with this event’s recorded status because the necessary event evidence is unavailable. The source timestamp has no timezone designation.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_71918067bc67/audit-report.json` and submitted; the report remains **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
